course: dictionary
lesson: 14829
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look the same but mean different things. The word ra is one of them. Its meaning depends on the context, which means the words and sentences around it. Look at the clues before you decide what it means.
explain: A capital letter is a clue too. «Ra was the sun god of ancient Egypt.» Ra has a capital R because it is the name of a god. When you see RA in capitals, it is often a short form for a longer name, such as the Royal Academy of Arts.
explain: Lowercase ra, or rah, is often a cheering shout. «The crowd shouted, "Rah, rah, rah!" as the team ran out.» The shout shows excitement and support. Ask yourself: does the sentence sound like a name, a short form, or a shout?
fact: Ra was the sun god of ancient Egypt, often shown with a falcon's head and the sun disc on top.
fact: Egyptians believed Ra sailed across the sky in a boat each day, and through the underworld each night.
fact: Ra is the chemical symbol for radium, a radioactive element.
fact: RA can stand for the Royal Academy of Arts, a resident assistant in a US college dorm, or rheumatoid arthritis, a joint illness.
fact: "Rah" or "ra" is a cheering shout, as in "rah-rah".
exercise: «Ra was the sun god of ancient Egypt.» What is Ra in this sentence? | *A sun god of ancient Egypt | A helper in a college dorm | A chemical element | A cheering shout
exercise: «Ra is the chemical symbol for radium.» What does Ra mean in this sentence? | A god of the sun | A cheer for a team | *A chemical symbol for radium | A kind of joint illness
exercise: «She is an RA in her college dorm, helping new students settle in.» What does RA stand for here? | Radium | Rheumatoid arthritis | *Resident assistant | Royal Academy of Arts
test: «The crowd roared, "Rah, rah, rah!" as the team ran onto the pitch.» What is rah in this sentence? | A kind of joint illness | Ancient Egyptian god | *A cheering shout | Chemical symbol for radium
test: Why is Ra written with a capital R in «Pharaohs were called "son of Ra"»? | It is at the start of a sentence | It is a cheering shout | It is a short form for a longer name | *It is the name of a god
exam: In «Grandma's hands ache, and the doctor says it is RA, a joint illness», what does RA stand for? | Resident assistant | Royal Academy of Arts | *Rheumatoid arthritis | Radium
